# Generated outputs (synthetic, but kept out of versioning as a matter of hygiene)
out/
*.zip
# Exception: the demo sample IS versioned
!samples/*.zip

# JS dependencies installed at the root (the web package already has its own rule)
node_modules/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# OS / editors
.DS_Store

# Claude Code — ignored whole. The launch config names the private Instagram sandbox below, so
# tracking it would publish a pointer into a directory this file deliberately excludes. To be
# revisited when that connector lands in web/ and the path becomes public.
.claude/

# Raw session transcripts (private) — only the curated AI_USAGE.md entry is public
transcripts/

# Instagram (v2) — private R&D sandbox: contains a real export, under consent.
# A real export may feed the work, it never enters the repo (invariant, CLAUDE.md).
# What comes out of it can only be a structure or a statistic — never a value.
#
# ⚠ THE LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. Without it the pattern matches a directory of that name at
# ANY depth — and `core.ignorecase` is true on macOS, so it also matched `web/public/guides/
# instagram/`. The fourteen screenshots of the Instagram export guide were silently never staged:
# `git add -A` reported nothing, the page worked locally off the working tree, and production would
# have served fourteen 404s. Anchored, it means this directory and only this one.
/Instagram/

# Benchmark runs from old R&D tooling (the WebLLM playground, since removed). Nothing produces them
# any more, but runs may survive locally: they contain inference output on real data and must never
# be committed (privacy invariant, CLAUDE.md).
benchmark-runs/
Design.pdf

# Structure quiz — a personal tool for re-reading the project (bus factor of 1, METHODE.md).
# Nothing in it is produced by the product or consumed by it: the question banks are a hand-written
# snapshot, and progress lives in the browser's localStorage.
quiz/

# Geo databases — fetched by `web/scripts/fetch-geo-db.mjs`, never committed (~40 MB, monthly
# re-publication). Their absence is a degraded mode, not a failure: cf. NOTICE.
/web/public/geo/
